        "source": "2022_10_14.md",
        "title": "Updates",
        "content": "### Feature Updates\n\n* We have added the option to edit condition nodes with existing connections, so that they don't get deleted while editing a node. It is possible to add or remove conditions, which results in changing existing connections, so before saving a Flow, you need to make sure it is built correctly. Changing the condition type deletes all existing connections and requires connecting the condition from scratch.\n\n### GUI Updates\n\n* We have introduced new columns: **Brand**, **Model**, **Operating System**, **Operating System version**, **Browser** and **Browser versions** to the device-related part of the User Sessions table in **Reporting > Statistics > Raw Data**.\n* A new pie chart **Device Brands** has been added to **Reporting > Statistics > Wi-Fi Users**. It presents the percentage breakdown of the device brands with which users connect to the WiFi.\n* We have removed the COVID-19 badge for **Density alerting** from the left menu.\n\n### System Updates\n\n* Due to a stricter security policy, our API no longer accepts cross-origin requests. See <https://web.dev/cross-origin-resource-sharing/> for a thorough explanation of the topic.\n* We have added mechanisms that clean up leftover WiFi User data when an organisation is deleted.",
